{title: 289 - The Savior Is Waiting}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #289 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 289}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]The Savior is waiting [Gb]to [Gm]enter your heart
[C7]Why [F/C]don't [C7]you let Him come [F]in?
[F]There's nothing in this world to [Gb]keep you apart
[Gm]What is your answer [C7]to Him?
[C7]Time after time He [F]has [Bb]waited before
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Gm]Time after [Am]time
[Am]He has [Dm]waited [Gm]before
[C7/E]And now [Dm]He is [C7]waiting [F]again
[F]To [Bb]see if you [Gm]are willing
[Am]To [C7]open [Gm]the door
[C7]Oh, how He wants to come [F]in.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]If you'll take [Gb]one [Gm]step
[C7]Toward the Savior, my [F]friend,
[F]You'll find His arms open [Gb]wide.
[Gm]Receive Him, and all of [C7]your darkness will end
[C7]Within your [F]heart [Bb]He'll abide.
{end_of_verse}
